# LF everywhere, on every machine, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Terraform zips the Lambda handlers straight from the working copy, so line
# endings are part of each function's code hash. With autocrlf on Windows the
# handlers had CRLF; a Linux CI runner checks out LF. The same commit then
# built different zips in the two places, and each apply would redeploy all
# six Lambdas over bytes nobody can see.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
